  "conclusions": [
    "For each app, RTM-labelled and Windows95C extraction executables are byte-identical.",
    "For each app, all three extraction sets have identical .text and .rsrc hashes, including menus/dialogs/strings.",
    "OSR1-labelled files have different full hashes/import data; do not infer new visible features from that alone.",
    "No per-release application UI fork is justified by this evidence. Shared controls, fonts, colors, locale and runtime DLL versions require separate comparison."
